<commit message="Fix flow visualization for items inside room placements

- Remove composite keys from _building_items/_belt_items (rooms only exist once in data model)
- Iterate room items directly in update_flow_visualization, set_show_flow_rates, set_show_efficiency
- Each visual item uses its flow_key (placement_id:item_id) to look up flow solver results
- This correctly displays flow rates/efficiency for items inside blueprints"/>

Done! The fix:
1. Removes the composite key tracking in `_building_items`/`_belt_items` - items use simple IDs since rooms only exist once in the data model
2. Updates `update_flow_visualization`, `set_show_flow_rates`, and `set_show_efficiency` to explicitly iterate over items inside room placements
3. Each visual item uses its `flow_key` property to look up flow solver results (which includes `placement_id` for items inside rooms)
